# .scripts

Tooling for the vault. Hidden from Obsidian (dot-folder), not notes.

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `vault-lint` | Validator for `Agents/` rules, plus the GTD review for agents without Obsidian. Python 3 stdlib only. |
| `import-files` | Vault intake helper: `inventory` (every file in `_imports/` and `_captures/` with size, type, sha256, duplicate or new, note or foreign, code flags), `file --src --slug --name [--dry-run]` (moves byte for byte into `_files/<slug>/`, or `_attachments/<slug>/` when the store is locked or absent; manifest row; checksum check; prints the embed path; a duplicate gets a row and no move), `done-capture <path>`, `fence-fix <path>`. Never deletes an original. Tests: `tests/test_import_files.py`. |
| `tidy-check` | Read-only vault docs pre-pass (Tidy mode): orphans, duplicate-looking titles and aliases, today's new Resources and People as a `Tidy <Mon D> imports` list, and their broken links. |
| `run-log` | `start <agent> "<asked>"` writes the run-log heading; `end <agent> [--summary ...]` appends Summary and `### Checks` with lint before and after counts. |
| `vault-brief` | Daily review as Markdown from `vault-lint --review --json` (`--snapshot-facts` lists facts the Home snapshot could cite). Read-only. |
| `sort-inbox` | Read-only inbox pre-pass: answered question tasks, tasks with explicit signals, tasks needing judgment. |
| `pm-check <project-slug>` | Read-only project check: phase, open tasks, next-action rule, best queued task to promote, stale waiting-for, overdue. |
| `tests/` | Fixture vaults and the test runner for `vault-lint` (`run.py`); the script tests are `test_*.py` beside it (`python3 -m unittest discover -s .scripts/tests`). |
[[% if store %]]
| `store-move` | moves filed attachments into the file store (`_files/`), checking checksums and repointing links. `--dry-run` first. Rules: `Agents/organization.md` (File store). |
| `store-image` | `status`, `unlock`, `lock` for the file store's encrypted disk image. Agents check `status` before writing to `_files/`. |
[[% endif %]]
[[% if pii %]]
| `pii-register-check` | Needs the 1Password CLI (`op`) signed in: checks the PII register document against `Resources/pii-register.md` (every key both ways), and with a file argument that the file is byte-identical. Prints keys and checksums, never values. |
| `pii-merge-queue` | Needs the 1Password CLI (`op`) signed in: merges `_files/_private/pii-register-queue.md` into the register document under each person's heading, asks before uploading, skips keys already there, removes exact duplicate rows (lists same-key conflicts), checks every key landed, then offers to empty the queue. `--dry-run` shows the plan. Prints keys and counts, never values. |
[[% endif %]]
[[% if backup %]]
| `restic/` | Nightly restic backups of the vault[[%+ if store +%]] and the file store[[%+ endif +%]]. See `restic/README.md`. |
[[% endif %]]

## vault-lint

```sh
python3 .scripts/vault-lint                    # lint the whole vault
python3 .scripts/vault-lint Tasks/ Home.md     # only report these paths
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --only links,tasks # only these checks
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --quiet            # errors only
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --json             # [{check, severity, path, line, message, fixable}]
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --fix              # safe frontmatter fixes + Linter body formatting, then re-lint
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --fix Tasks/x.md   # the same, for one changed file (the usual agent step)
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --list-checks
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --today 2026-10-01 # pretend it's another day (date rules)
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --archive-closed --promote --dry-run   # the plan, nothing written
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --archive-closed --promote             # do it
```

Exit `0` = no errors (warnings and info never fail), `1` = errors, `2` = bad usage.
The whole vault is always indexed, so a path filter only narrows what's reported.
A whole-vault run takes about 0.2 s.

Checks, in output order: `structure`, `file-format`, `frontmatter-present`,
`frontmatter-syntax`, `filename`, `unique-names`, `title`, `schema`, `links`,
`relations`, `waiting-on`, `tasks`, `projects`, `archive`, `attachments`, `manifest`, `anatomy`,
`dataview`, `dataviewjs`, `dates`, `pii`, `sensitive`, `format`, `orphans`, `facts`, `source-urls`. A check whose module is off in `.tidyvault.yml` is skipped (`--list-checks` says which).

`--fix` only does rewrites that can't change meaning: key order, quoting bare
wikilinks, inline → block lists, list indent, unquoting ISO dates, deleting
empty keys and the redundant retired fields (`agent_review`, `edited`, `archive: false`,
and `lint.retired_fields` from `.tidyvault.yml`), and stripping a UTF-8 byte-order mark.
Key order is `title` → folder fields → (Archive: `archived`, `archived_from`) →
`aliases`, `tags`, `sensitive`, `public_places`, `created`.

In the body it applies the `format` check, the same spacing and markup the
Obsidian Linter writes on save: trailing spaces, `*`/`+`/`•` bullets to `-`,
one blank line around headings, code fences, tables and blockquotes, no runs of
blank lines, no blank line between the frontmatter and the H1, one newline at
end of file.

`--fix` guarantees:

- **Wording never changes.** Body fixes touch only whitespace and markup, never
  fenced code. CRLF notes and templates get frontmatter fixes only; their
  bodies are left byte for byte.
- **Atomic:** each file is written to a temp file in the same folder, fsynced,
  and renamed over the original with its mode kept. If the file changed on disk
  since it was read (another agent, Obsidian), it is skipped, not clobbered.
- **Idempotent:** a second run changes nothing.
- **Hands off** anything it can't rewrite safely: frontmatter outside the YAML
  subset, mixed line endings in the frontmatter, non-UTF-8 files, symlinks,
  files over 2 MB. Fix those by hand.

Odd files never crash a run: non-UTF-8 files are decoded with replacement and
reported (`file-format` error); BOM and CRLF are reported and handled; symlinks
are reported and never followed (they still resolve as link targets); notes over
2 MB are reported and skipped by content checks.

Exempt: `Agents/templates/` note bodies (Templater source) and the root files
`AGENTS.md` and `llms.txt` (not vault notes; they still count
for `unique-names`). Project rules follow the state machine in `Agents/gtd.md`.

Never indexed: hidden dot-folders, `_tmp/` (agent scratch space), `_imports/`
(foreign files awaiting import), and `_captures/` (capture notes awaiting
filing); rules for all three are in
`Agents/organization.md`. Nothing inside them is linted, counted for
`unique-names`, or used to resolve links, so a stray copy there can't break a run.

`schema.md` is the contract. When it changes, update the tables at the top of
`vault-lint` in the same change. The docstring explains how to add a check.

## Archive and promote (the mechanical GTD steps)

Two flags do what an agent used to do by hand, with no tokens spent. Both print
one line per change, run `--fix` on the files they wrote, then lint. `--dry-run`
prints the plan and writes nothing. Paths limit what they touch.

| Flag | Does | Leaves for an agent |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--archive-closed` | Every `done` or `cancelled` task in `Tasks/`: sets `completed` (today, when missing), adds `archived: true` and `archived_from: Tasks`, moves it to `Archive/` under the same filename (`Agents/procedures.md`, Archive a file) | Closed projects (archiving sorts their tasks and Resources); a task whose frontmatter is outside the subset; a filename already taken in `Archive/` |
| `--promote` | Each `not-started` or `in-progress` project with no next action: sets its best `queued` task with every blocker closed to `next-action`; best = highest `priority`, then earliest `due`, then oldest `created` (`Agents/gtd.md`, Promote on close) | `contexts` (never guessed; the report flags a promoted task without them); a project with no ready queued task (write one, or change its phase) |

Neither overwrites anything: a name taken in `Archive/`, or a file that changed
while the script ran, is skipped and reported. Together, archive runs first. The
`--review` "Promote" pointer under "Projects breaking the next-action rule" uses
the same rule.

## Review mode (GTD review without Obsidian)

Agents that can't run Dataview use this instead of the queries in
`Agents/gtd.md`:

```sh
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --review                     # Markdown, today
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --review --today 2026-10-01  # as of another day
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --review --days 7            # daily review: due within 2 days, plus the week ahead
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --review --json              # one object, a key per section
python3 .scripts/vault-lint --review --no-git            # staleness from file mtimes, not git
```

Sections, in order (JSON keys in brackets):

| Section | What it lists |
| --- | --- |
| Lint summary [`lint`] | Error and warning counts from a full lint |
| Overdue and due within N days [`due`] | Open tasks and active projects with `due` ≤ today + `--days` (default 7), with days left or overdue |
| Next actions by project [`next_actions_by_project`] | `next-action` tasks grouped by `project` (`""` = area-only), sorted by due, priority, created |
| Next actions by context [`next_actions_by_context`] | The same tasks grouped by each `contexts` value (`""` = none set) |
| Inbox captures [`inbox`, `queued_steps`] | `inbox` tasks, oldest first; count of `queued` project steps |
| Waiting for [`waiting`] | Every `waiting-for` task with its age in days; 7+ days (or no `waiting_since`) is flagged "chase, wait, or drop?" |
| Next-action rule breaches [`project_rule`] | Projects outside the state machine's next-action count, with the next action to promote when one is missing |
| Blocked tasks to promote [`promote`] | `inbox` or `queued` tasks whose every `blocked_by` is done, cancelled, or archived |
| Stale projects [`stale_projects`] | `in-progress` projects with no change to any of their tasks (in `Tasks/` or `Archive/`) for 14+ days, from `git log`; uncommitted edits count as today. Falls back to file mtimes when the vault isn't a git work-tree root or git is missing (`source` says which) |
| Closed but not archived [`closed_not_archived`] | `done`/`cancelled` tasks and projects still in `Tasks/` or `Projects/` |
| Someday/maybe revisits [`revisit`] | Bullets under an Area's `## Someday/maybe` whose `(revisit YYYY-MM-DD)` is on or before today |

Review mode always exits `0` and never writes.

